# Week 1 — GitHub and Pages
Create a repository named `web-development-experiments` under `krititayal`, add `index.html` and `style.css`, then try the workflow below. Push the feature branch, open a pull request on GitHub, review and merge it. Enable Pages in Settings → Pages from `main`. Save your published URL and a screenshot for the lab record.

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Add landing page"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/krititayal/web-development-experiments.git
git push -u origin main
git switch -c docs/landing-page
# make a small edit, then:
git add . && git commit -m "Update landing page"
git push -u origin docs/landing-page
```
